If one of the four components of a start-up’s business model doesn’t take
shape, the entire business model can fail. This is what happened to iContact,
a company that was started to build a mobile social network. While its core
strategy, strategic resources, and customer interface were strong, the firm
couldn’t motivate its key partners to cooperate, causing it to fail, as illustrated

