business model. Some firms differentiate their products or services and
provide extra value to their customers through high levels of service and
support. Customer service can include delivery and installation, financing
arrangements, customer training, warranties and guarantees, repairs,
layaway plans, convenient hours of operation, convenient parking, and infor-
mation through toll-free numbers and Web sites.*! Dell, as mentioned
earlier, has a broad menu of tiered services available to provide its corporate
clients the exact level of support they need and for which they are willing to
pay. Making this choice of services available is a key component of Dell’s
business model.

